Forked content
--------------

The file patterns.ts in this directory is a faithful TypeScript port of the
upstream patterns.py at the commit above. The pattern data — 25 regex,
substring and argument-aware rules covering unsafe deserialization, command
injection, XSS sinks, crypto footguns, XXE, GitHub Actions injection, and
TLS-verification disablement — is unmodified in substance.

Three upstream refinements are carried across in the port:

- Browser DOM rules (innerHTML, outerHTML, insertAdjacentHTML,
  dangerouslySetInnerHTML, document.write) and `new Function` only fire in
  JS/TS files.
- `eval()` skips Playwright/Puppeteer `page.$eval('selector', function)`,
  which runs the function rather than evaluating a string.
- `yaml.load`, `torch.load` and `numpy.load` read their own arguments across
  lines and nested brackets, so a `SafeLoader` / `weights_only=True` /
  `allow_pickle=True` further into the call is seen (upstream's `_call_args`).

